From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:49:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [QW38] gdn recover fold test: zero recycled boundary blocks
 in both paths

A block recycled from a finished request holds stale state that legitimately
differs between eager and deferred commit (the last records of a finished
request are never folded); nothing reads it before a boundary store. The
align-mode boundary check compared that stale content (7/8 align cases).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py b/tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py
index 6566ca494..f778066e4 100644
--- a/tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py
+++ b/tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py
@@ -167,6 +167,12 @@ class _Sim:
                 b = self.rng.choice(self.free_slots)
                 self.free_slots.remove(b)
                 r.blocks.append(b)
+                # A recycled block holds stale content, which legitimately
+                # differs between the paths (a finished request's last
+                # records are never folded); nothing reads it before a
+                # boundary store, so start both copies from the same bits.
+                for s in self.ref_states + self.fold_states + (self.prev_ref or []):
+                    s[b].zero_()
 
     # ---- graph mode ------------------------------------------------------------
     def _init_graph(self):
